  instructions: "Use the qualified independent mesh-repair provider on the exact upstream source mesh. Preserve that source. Record before/after dimensions, topology, feature preservation, triangle count and every geometry change with units. Do not erase required holes, recesses, blends or contact faces to make repair pass. Retain a closed printable mesh and the repair report. Fail clearly if repair would violate the reviewed specification. Preparation here grants no strength acceptance or printer permission."
  settings: {"authoring_template":"mcp-task","mcp_server":"import:draft-92ea6423d17519e26dc7","mcp_task_tools":["execute_blender_code"],"max_tool_calls":6,"timeout_seconds":300,"output_format":"json","save_output":true,"output_filename":"results/{{wright.run_id}}/mesh-repair/{{wright.producer_attempt}}/repair-report.json","file_policy":"indexed","run_path_template":"wright.run-path/2","revision_policy":"create_new_files","expected_files":"results/{{wright.run_id}}/mesh-repair/{{wright.producer_attempt}}/repaired.stl","expected_file_ports":{"mesh_repair_repaired":"results/{{wright.run_id}}/mesh-repair/{{wright.producer_attempt}}/repaired.stl"},"task_guidance":"Use only the selected independent Blender execute_blender_code tool with safe mode enabled. The exact current workspace is mounted at /workspace. Import only the upstream source mesh and preserve its original bytes. Use supported native STL import/export operators and allowed bpy/bmesh operations; do not disable safe mode, use raw sockets or load arbitrary scripts. Keep the user's quoted task in user_prompt. Record import-time topology changes as well as explicit repair operations, before/after dimensions in millimetres, topology, component count, volume and feature-preservation findings in the response report. Preserve required holes, recesses, blends and contact faces. Export to the exact attempt-scoped repaired.stl path under /workspace, never overwrite a previous result. The report must distinguish observations from checks not performed; unsupported checks remain unresolved. If repair changes reviewed design geometry or invalidates the upstream strength assessment, report blocked and require a new CAD/analysis revision. Provider success and this report do not replace the downstream independent geometry and analysis-applicability checks."}
  tool: null
  reusable_step: null
end

